last year brazil faced the worst forest  fires in a decade  but 2021 could be worse according to  data released  by brazil's national institute for space  research  during the first five months of the year  more than 2  500 square kilometers of amazon  rainforest  have been destroyed it's an area three  times the size of new york city  and half of it was destroyed in may with  charts  showing some of the worst damage since  2015.  compared to the same month last year  deforestation has risen by 67 percent  if nothing changes this year could be  even worse than 2020.  besides the surge in deforestation  brazil is facing a drought  brazil's president jair bolsonaro has  never made the amazon a priority  but after his ally donald trump was  defeated by joe biden through the u.s  presidential elections  he bowed down to international pressure  at april's climate change summit  hosted by biden bolsonaro pledged to  invest more  in environmental enforcement but many in  brazil warned biden  that brazil's government would take no  action to stop wild cat miners  loggers and farmers from destroying the  rainforest  among them 90 year old indigenous tribe  leader hao ni  we got away if this bad president says  something to you  ignore him he wants to allow our forest  to be destroyed by encouraging invasions  on our land  and i don't like it bolsonaro's  government has been accused of weakening  institutions and legislation protecting  the rainforest and the indigenous people  the 2021 federal budget further cut  environmental spending  and brazil's environment minister  jukartasanis  is being investigated for allegedly  obstructing a probe into illegal logging  brazil's vice president emil tomorrow  says bolsonaro will deploy the army once  more to protect the amazon  but environmentalists say the government  must act fast  if it really wants to prevent a disaster  meanwhile land grabbers are losing no  time in may more than 1  300 kilometers of the amazon rainforest  was chopped down  most of the destruction has been caused  by speculators who invade  government-owned land to clear it  they hope to legalize it and sell it at  a good price for cattle and farmers  for land grabbers the chance is now next  year brazil will hold presidential  elections  and bolsonaro may not win a second term  monica yanagiv al jazeera rio de janeiro
 

